CORE
integer-operators.c

Passing problem to incremental SMT2 solving
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 8 a - b > 0: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 10 -a < 0: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line 12 b <= a: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line 13 a >= b: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Exercises mathematical-integer (__CPROVER_integer) subtraction, unary minus and
the relational operators in the incremental SMT2 back-end (smt_integer_theoryt).
Division and modulo are intentionally not yet supported (deferred; SMT-LIB Int
div/mod are Euclidean whereas mod_exprt/div_exprt truncate toward zero).
